  "project_description": "Views Json Source is an extension of views module to work with external JSON data. Any JSON API can be configured to render the data directly from the JSON through views. The json content is not stored in Drupal.\n\n HOW IT WORKS \n \n When creating a view choose \"Json\" on \"Show\" field. \n Then when editing the view, In \"Advanced\" section, click \"Settings\" on \"Query settings\",\n\nchoose the source of the Json data, define the row apath and you're done. \n Add one or more fields and set the key value of the field you want to show. \n Optional : Add any filters or sort criteria as required. \n Optional : Make use of Contextual filters as required.",
